---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
import '../styles/pages.css';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

// Counted from the collection, not typed in — the same reason the affiliate
// disclosure computes itself: a hand-written number goes stale silently.
const entries = await getCollection('tools');
const toolCount = entries.length;
const sourceCount = entries.reduce((n, e) => n + e.data.sources.length, 0);
const lastVerified = new Date(
  Math.max(...entries.map((e) => e.data.lastVerified.getTime()))
).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---

<Base
  title="About — AgentLife"
  description="How AgentLife picks and ranks AI tools: one consistent rubric, refreshed monthly, and independent of who pays us."
>
  <main class="page">
    <section class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:3rem">About</p>
      <h1>How AgentLife works</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        AgentLife helps busy people find the AI tools that actually fit how they
        work — a few quick questions instead of a giant, unranked list.
      </p>

      <div class="facts">
        <div>
          <div class="fact-value">{toolCount}</div>
          <div class="fact-label">tools scored on one rubric</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="fact-value">{sourceCount}</div>
          <div class="fact-label">sources cited across them</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="fact-value">{lastVerified}</div>
          <div class="fact-label">last full re-check</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How we rank tools</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool is scored against the same rubric: how good it is at each
        task, and how much of the work it can take off your hands. We match that
        against what you tell us — your task, how hands-off you want to be, how
        much setup you'll tolerate, and whether you want free options — so
        results are picked for <em>you</em>, not one-size-fits-all.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don't publish a match percentage. With a handful of genuinely capable
        tools per task, a number like &ldquo;93% match&rdquo; implies a precision
        we can't honestly claim. Instead each recommendation gets a role it
        earned — <em>our pick</em>, <em>best free option</em>, <em>easiest to
        start with</em> — and the reason it earned it. When two tools are too
        close to separate, we say that instead of inventing a winner. When no
        tool earns a role, we leave it out rather than pad the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Kept current</h2>
      <p>
        The whole list is reviewed every month — an AI-assisted pass that we
        check by hand — so pricing and features stay accurate, discontinued
        tools drop off, and strong new ones get added. Each tool carries the
        date it was last reviewed.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />

      <h2>Suggest a tool</h2>
      <p>
        Think we've missed something great? We review every suggestion against
        the same criteria — neither being suggested nor running an affiliate
        program earns a spot. (A submission form is on its way.)
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Layout comes from pages.css (.prose / .facts); only the page's own
     trailing spacing lives here. */
  .prose {
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }
</style>
